# Secrets - never reach GitHub

## Hard ban

Never add to the repo (code, docs, screenshots of env, commit messages, or agent notes):

- API tokens, PATs, shared secrets, webhook secrets
- Private keys / PEM / OpenSSH / `*.pem` / `id_rsa` / keystores
- Passwords or `user:pass@host` URLs
- `.env` and any real environment values
- Private or loopback IPs (`10.*`, `192.168.*`, `172.16-31.*`, `127.*`, `169.254.*`)
- Internal hostnames (`*.internal`, `*.corp`, `*.lan`)

## Allowed

- Public site origin in `src/lib/site.ts` (`https://lamoursucre.com`)
- Public third-party marketing URLs (Instagram, etc.)
- Placeholder text only: `CHANGE_ME`, `process.env.*`, `<YOUR_TOKEN>`

## Agent behaviour

- Prefer `.env.example` with empty / placeholder values; never real values
- If a secret appears in context, do not write it into any tracked file
- Do not suggest `--no-verify` to bypass `scripts/check-no-secrets.sh`
- Details: `docs/SECURITY.md`
